                <pb facs="0770" n="668" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg668"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 847/142.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister for Foreign Affairs of
                            Panama to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Panama</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1908-10-03"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">October 3,
                    1908</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Profoundly thankful for your excellency’s felicitations. I avail myself of the
                    opportunity to express my hope that the relations of our two countries may ever
                    be as close and cordial as they have been heretofore.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Arango.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
